# TASK 1: Literature Review on Drug Development

## 1. Selected Drug
* **Drug Name:** Semaglutide (FDA-approved within the last 5 years as a breakthrough treatment for Type 2 Diabetes and Obesity)[span_0](start_span)[span_0](end_span).

## 2. Drug Discovery Process
* **Identification & Analog Design:** Developed as an analog of human glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1), engineered to resist degradation by the dipeptidyl peptidase-4 (DPP-4) enzyme[span_1](start_span)[span_1](end_span).
* **Structural Modification:** A fatty diacid chain was attached to the peptide backbone, allowing strong binding to serum albumin and ensuring a prolonged half-life suitable for once-weekly subcutaneous administration[span_2](start_span)[span_2](end_span).

## 3. Clinical Trial Phases
* **Preclinical Development:** Extensive in vitro and in vivo pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic evaluations to test receptor affinity and glucose-dependent insulinotropic effects[span_3](start_span)[span_3](end_span).
* **Clinical Trials (SUSTAIN & STEP Programs):** 
  * *Phase I & II:* Evaluated safety, tolerability, and dose-ranging parameters in healthy volunteers and patients with Type 2 diabetes[span_4](start_span)[span_4](end_span).
  * *Phase III:* Large-scale multi-center trials comparing efficacy against placebo and active comparators, demonstrating superior glycemic control (HbA1c reduction) and significant weight loss[span_5](start_span)[span_5](end_span).

## 4. Therapeutic Applications
* Management of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control[span_6](start_span)[span_6](end_span).
* Chronic weight management in adults with obesity or overweight with at least one weight-related comorbidity[span_7](start_span)[span_7](end_span).
* Risk reduction of major adverse cardiovascular events (cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial infarction, or non-fatal stroke) in patients with Type 2 diabetes and established cardiovascular disease[span_8](start_span)[span_8](end_span).

